Record each derivation a state turns into its outPath.

A store path in an evaluated string names a derivation output, but not
the value it came from. Module code writes `"${pkg}"`, and the string
keeps only `pkg.outPath` and its context. `meta` (licenses, CPEs,
homepage) lives on the value, so an SBOM of what an evaluation ships
had to find the value again by guessing attribute names. On a
Kubernetes environment that matched 403 of 1007 store paths
(nixidae/nixidae#1373).

The evaluator holds the value at the moment it coerces it.
`setRecordDerivations(true)` makes every later coercion of a
derivation to its outPath record outPath -> value in the state: string
coercion (`"${drv}"`, `toString`, a derivation's environment) and
`toJSON` (structured attributes). The record is a root, so the values
live as long as the state or until `clearRecordedDerivations`.

Off by default: a state that does not record pays one relaxed atomic
load per coercion. Recording changes no result and throws nothing new:
an error while it checks the value is left to the caller's own force.

diff --git a/src/libexpr/eval.cc b/src/libexpr/eval.cc
index cc5bd97..51b3149 100644
--- a/src/libexpr/eval.cc
+++ b/src/libexpr/eval.cc
@@ -2544,6 +2544,63 @@ bool EvalState::isDerivation(Value & v)
     return i->value->string_view().compare("derivation") == 0;
 }
 
+void EvalState::setRecordDerivations(bool record)
+{
+    recordingDerivations.store(record, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+}
+
+void EvalState::clearRecordedDerivations()
+{
+    std::lock_guard lock(recordedDerivationsMutex);
+    recordedDerivations.clear();
+}
+
+void EvalState::noteDerivationOutPath(Value & drv, Value & outPath, const PosIdx pos)
+{
+    if (!recordingDerivations.load(std::memory_order_relaxed))
+        return;
+    /* Recording must not change what evaluation does. `isDerivation`
+       forces `type`, which a coercion does not. An error is left to the
+       caller's own force of `outPath`, which throws it with its trace. */
+    try {
+        forceValue(outPath, pos);
+        if (outPath.type() != nString || !isDerivation(drv))
+            return;
+    } catch (Error &) {
+        return;
+    }
+    auto path = outPath.string_view();
+    {
+        std::lock_guard lock(recordedDerivationsMutex);
+        if (recordedDerivations.contains(path))
+            return;
+    }
+    /* `drv` may be a copy on the caller's stack. The attribute set it
+       points at is in collector memory, so a copy of the value holds the
+       same derivation. */
+    auto copy = allocValue();
+    *copy = drv;
+    std::lock_guard lock(recordedDerivationsMutex);
+    recordedDerivations.try_emplace(std::string(path), copy);
+}
+
+Value * EvalState::recordedDerivation(std::string_view outPath)
+{
+    std::lock_guard lock(recordedDerivationsMutex);
+    auto i = recordedDerivations.find(outPath);
+    return i == recordedDerivations.end() ? nullptr : i->second;
+}
+
+std::vector<std::string> EvalState::recordedOutPaths()
+{
+    std::lock_guard lock(recordedDerivationsMutex);
+    std::vector<std::string> paths;
+    paths.reserve(recordedDerivations.size());
+    for (auto & [path, _] : recordedDerivations)
+        paths.push_back(path);
+    return paths;
+}
